{# STEP 2 — WHAT HAPPENED.

   TWO OF THE THREE RULED REQUIREMENTS LIVE HERE: one line saying what happened,
   and the place. They are marked, and only they are — how bad it was, when, and
   the reporter's own words are offered in the same breath as "or later on the
   record", because a figure guessed at the roadside is worse than none and the
   append-only timeline records who added what and when either way.

   WHAT HAPPENED IS A TEXTAREA, not a one-line field. What somebody writes at the
   roadside is a sentence, and a note copied in from an observation is routinely
   longer than a single line — so the box grows to fit what is in it rather than
   scrolling a sentence sideways past a cursor. The caption says what is true of
   the consequence: every listing in this module is a row, so the REGISTER SHOWS
   THE FIRST LINE ({@see \Uhifadhi\Incident\Entity\Incident::headline()}) while
   the whole answer is kept and shown on the case file.

   IT ARRIVES ANSWERED WHEN THE FILING CAME FROM A RECORD. The source record's
   note is put straight into it — the person filing has already written what
   happened once, and asking them to write it again is the surest way to get a
   report that never exists. It is fully editable, and the SOURCE CARD above still
   shows the note verbatim, so editing this never touches the original. A long
   note is prefilled whole and the field's own limit shows rather than silently
   losing the end of it.

   THE SHARED ANSWERS ARE ASKED ONCE. What happened, where, when, how bad and the
   verbatim note belong to every kind of incident, so they are asked once, above
   the swapped field sets — never sixteen times with fifteen of them disabled.

   STEP 2 IS THEN THE SUB-CATEGORY'S OWN, AND ITS QUESTIONS COME FROM ITS BLOCKS.
   One fold per behaviour block the word switched on, in the kinds editor's order,
   drawn by @UhifadhiIncident/report/_blocks.html.twig from the catalogue — nothing
   on this page types a question. Every sub-category's step 2 is rendered and all
   but the chosen one are hidden AND disabled, so the posted form carries only what
   the chosen word actually asks. The MONEY fold exists only where the
   sub-category carries money — choose a natural mortality and there is no money
   question in the document at all. Not disabled. Absent.

   The page writes the one line on a labelled row, in the same field set as where,
   when and how bad — one column with room for a caption under each answer.

   EVERYTHING IS DRAWN FROM `answers`: the hand-off's guesses on a fresh form,
   and what was posted on a form that came back, so a refusal never costs the
   filer what they had written.

   Parameters: controller, momentController, kinds, chosen, prefill, answers, blockSets, areaLists, placement, placementKept
   ========================================================================== #}
<div class="i-fieldset">
    <div class="i-fld"><label for="report-title">What happened</label>
        <span><textarea id="report-title" name="title" maxlength="200" rows="2"
                        placeholder="What happened — the list shows the first line"
                        {{ stimulus_target(controller, 'headline')|stimulus_action(controller, 'grow', 'input') }}>{{ answers.title }}</textarea>
            <span class="ro-req">needed to file</span></span></div>

    {# THE PLACE — the one fact a report cannot be filed without and the one
       nobody can add reliably tomorrow. It arrives already answered when the
       filing came from a record, and stays editable because the record's guess
       is still a guess. #}
    <div {{ stimulus_target(controller, 'placement') }}>
        {{- include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_placement.html.twig', {controller: controller, placement: placement, placementKept: placementKept}, with_context: false) -}}
    </div>
    {# The area is asked where the point lies whenever either half of it changes. #}
    <div class="i-fld"><label for="report-lat">Where</label>
        <span><input type="text" id="report-lat" name="lat" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="latitude"
                     value="{{ answers.latitude }}" {{ stimulus_action(controller, 'place', 'input') }}>
            <input type="text" name="lng" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="longitude" aria-label="Longitude"
                   value="{{ answers.longitude }}" {{ stimulus_action(controller, 'place', 'input') }}>
            <span class="ro-req">needed to file</span>
            {% set where = include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_where.html.twig', {placement: placement}, with_context: false)|trim %}
            <span class="i-kpi-note" {{ stimulus_target(controller, 'where') }}{{ where is empty ? ' hidden' }}>{{ where|raw }}</span>
            {% if prefill.positionLabel %}<span class="i-kpi-note">{{ prefill.positionLabel }} · came with the {{ prefill.sourceLabel }}</span>{% endif %}</span></div>

    {# WHEN IT HAPPENED, IN THE READER'S OWN CLOCK.

       A `datetime-local` value has NO ZONE IN IT, so the same string means a
       different instant to every reader and a server that parses it in its own zone
       stores a moment nobody typed. So the page states both halves a reader cannot:
       the field is printed in UTC and carries on `data-instant` the instant it was
       filled from, and the hidden field carries the zone the browser says it is in.
       The controller converts the one and fills the other; the server reads the wall
       clock in that zone, and in UTC when the field is empty — which is what a
       reader with no JavaScript was shown. #}
    <div class="i-fld"><label for="report-when">When</label>
        <span {{ stimulus_controller(momentController) }}><input type="datetime-local" id="report-when" name="occurred_at"
                     {{ stimulus_target(momentController, 'input') }}
                     {% if answers.occurredAt %}data-instant="{{ answers.occurredAt|date('c') }}"{% endif %}
                     value="{{ answers.occurredAt ? answers.occurredAt|date('Y-m-d\\TH:i', 'UTC') }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="occurred_at_zone" value="" {{ stimulus_target(momentController, 'zone') }}>
            {% if prefill.occurredAt %}<span class="i-kpi-note">from the {{ prefill.sourceLabel }}</span>{% endif %}</span></div>

    {# SECONDARY, AND SAID SO. Present — because the person filing may well know —
       but never in the way of filing. #}
    <div class="i-fld"><label for="report-severity">How bad</label>
        <span><select class="fld" id="report-severity" name="severity">
                {%- for severity in ['low', 'moderate', 'high', 'critical'] %}
                <option value="{{ severity }}"{{ severity == answers.severity.value ? ' selected' }}>{{ severity }}</option>
                {%- endfor %}
            </select>
            <span class="ro-opt">can wait</span>
            <span class="i-kpi-note">defaults to moderate — whoever verifies it decides properly</span></span></div>

    <div class="i-fld"><label for="report-narrative">In their own words</label>
        <span><textarea id="report-narrative" name="narrative" rows="3"
                        placeholder="Verbatim — kept apart from the officer's assessment">{{ answers.narrative }}</textarea>
            <span class="ro-opt">can wait</span></span></div>
</div>

{# THE SUB-CATEGORY'S OWN QUESTIONS, one set per sub-category. #}
{% for kind in kinds %}
    {% for subcategory in kind.subcategories %}
        {% set isChosen = chosen and chosen.code == subcategory.code %}
        <div {{ stimulus_target(controller, 'fieldset') }}
             data-subcategory="{{ subcategory.code }}"{{ isChosen ? '' : ' hidden' }}>
        <div class="i-fieldset">
            <div class="hd">the questions {{ subcategory.label }} asks</div>

            {# The siblings under this kind. Choosing one swaps every question
               below, because the sub-category is what decides which blocks are on
               — and whether there is a money question at all. #}
            <div class="i-fld"><label>Sub-category</label>
                <span><span class="i-taxsub">
                    {%- for sibling in kind.subcategories -%}
                        <a href="#" class="{{ sibling.code == subcategory.code ? 'on' }}"
                           {{ stimulus_target(controller, 'category')|stimulus_action(controller, 'choose', 'click') }}
                           data-subcategory="{{ sibling.code }}"
                           data-subcategories="{{ sibling.code }}">{{ sibling.label }}</a>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                </span></span></div>

        </div>

        {# THE BLOCKS THIS WORD SWITCHED ON. A fold each, and the money fold only
           where the sub-category carries money — absent, never greyed. #}
        {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_blocks.html.twig', {
            controller: controller,
            sets: blockSets[subcategory.code]|default([]),
            subcategory: subcategory,
            areaLists: areaLists,
            disabled: not isChosen,
            answers: isChosen ? answers : null,
        }, with_context: false) }}
        </div>
    {% endfor %}
{% endfor %}

{# The chosen sub-category, as one value. The picker writes into it; without
   JavaScript the radios below carry it. #}
<input type="hidden" name="subcategory" value="{{ chosen ? chosen.code }}" data-incident-report-subcategory>
<noscript>
    <div class="i-fieldset">
        <div class="hd">what kind of incident</div>
        {% for kind in kinds %}
            {% for subcategory in kind.subcategories %}
                <div class="i-fld"><label><input type="radio" name="subcategory" value="{{ subcategory.code }}"
                    {{ chosen and chosen.code == subcategory.code ? 'checked' }}> {{ subcategory.path }}</label><span></span></div>
            {% endfor %}
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
</noscript>